  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "vendor-backend-still-built",
      "file": "drivers/soc/rockchip/Makefile",
      "line": 4,
      "detail": "sdmmc_vendor_storage.o is controlled by MMC_DW_ROCKCHIP, not ROCKCHIP_VENDOR_STORAGE. Disabling the latter does not remove the backend."
    },
    {
      "id": "vendor-backend-write-interface",
      "file": "drivers/soc/rockchip/sdmmc_vendor_storage.c",
      "lines": [
        398,
        577,
        595,
        608
      ],
      "detail": "The device initcall starts a thread that reads eMMC vendor records. Successful initialization registers /dev/vendor_storage; ioctls support vendor data and IDB writes. Initialization itself was not found to write vendor records in this C path."
    },
    {
      "id": "no-card-guard",
      "file": "drivers/mmc/host/rk_sdmmc_ops.c",
      "lines": [
        28,
        130,
        143
      ],
      "detail": "this_card starts NULL. rk_emmc_transfer returns -EIO before requesting I/O if no card is registered."
    },
    {
      "id": "emmc-card-registration",
      "file": "drivers/mmc/card/block.c",
      "lines": [
        2887,
        2888,
        2889
      ],
      "detail": "mmc_blk_probe assigns this_card only if the host restrict_caps includes RESTRICT_CARD_TYPE_EMMC. Generic SD and SDIO hosts are not assigned by this branch."
    },
    {
      "id": "host-capabilities-from-dtb",
      "file": "drivers/mmc/host/rk_sdmmc.c",
      "lines": [
        3442,
        3444,
        3446
      ],
      "detail": "supports-sd, supports-sdio and supports-emmc DT properties determine these host restriction bits."
    },
    {
      "id": "force-jtag-cleared-without-marker",
      "file": "drivers/mmc/host/rk_sdmmc.c",
      "lines": [
        3457,
        3458,
        3468,
        3469
      ],
      "detail": "Without rockchip_jtag_enabled, the RK322X branch clears force_jtag in RK322X_GRF_SOC_CON6. Keeping the inherited rockchip_jtag marker skips this branch."
    }
  ],
  "assessment": "With the intended DTB disabling the eMMC node and no other EMMC-capable active node, this_card is expected to stay NULL and backend I/O to return -EIO. This is conditional static evidence, not proof of physical flash preservation. Unknown module/init/bootloader paths remain unaudited."
